# PROJECT SANKET — ARCHITECTURAL RULES FOR CLINE

## Stack & Architecture
- Framework: Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Database: Supabase PostgreSQL with PostGIS extension (geography data types)
- Realtime: Supabase Realtime channel subscriptions over WebSockets
- Maps: React-Leaflet (MUST always be dynamically imported with { ssr: false } to prevent window undefined errors)
- AI: Google Gemini 2.5 Flash via REST API

## Strict Coding Constraints
1. Always run `npx tsc --noEmit` after modifying code to verify TypeScript integrity before declaring a task complete.
2. All Next.js Route Handlers (in `src/app/api/**/route.ts`) MUST include `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'`.
3. When updating the `Incident` interface, synchronize both `src/components/RescuerMap.tsx` and `src/app/rescuer/page.tsx` simultaneously to prevent TS2339 errors.
4. Keep the victim mobile bundle lightweight: ground evidence images must be compressed client-side to WebP (<35 KB) before database transmission.
